      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Goal 1:** 10,000 tx/s, sustained. **Goal 2:** 1,000,000 tx/s with a p99 of 1 ms from submit to the executed receipt.\n\n- *Executed tx/s* counts the applied transactions of the fastest executor. *Sustained* is the lowest 1-minute rate in 10 minutes.\n- *Submit to executed* starts at the ingress publish on `tx_data`, not at the HTTP request. The client also sees the network and the JSON-RPC time.\n- The latency histograms use the shared buckets of 100 \u00b5s to 5 s. A percentile is exact only to its bucket.\n- No panel shows the sealer's dedup window or its heap: the sealer has no scrape job yet.\n- CPU, memory and disk are on the Hosts and Nomad dashboards."
      }
